# HoKOS v1.4 - Smart Refresh Edition

Now supporting all high-refresh displays for Desktops, Laptops, and Tablets.

## Dynamic Support
- **High-End**: Native support for **185Hz** and **240Hz**.
- **Standard**: Optimized for **60Hz, 120Hz, 144Hz, 165Hz**.
- **Stability**: Locked **144FPS** for gaming to balance CPU/GPU load.
- **Cooling**: Intelligent thermal throttling to prevent overheating.

## Optimization
- Automatically detects hardware refresh rate.
- Sets Virtual Overdrive based on monitor capabilities.
#!/bin/bash
# HoKOS v1.4 - Universal Refresh Rate Setup
# Target: Laptop / PC / Tablet (No Mobile)
# Thermal-Aware Optimization

set -e

echo "[1/4] Detecting Hardware Refresh Rate..."

# Get current monitor refresh rate
CURRENT_HZ=$(xrandr | grep '*' | awk '{print $1}' | cut -d'x' -f2 | cut -d'.' -f1 | head -n1)
if [ -z "$CURRENT_HZ" ]; then CURRENT_HZ=60; fi

echo "Detected: ${CURRENT_HZ}Hz"

# Logic for Ultra-Smooth but Cool
if [ "$CURRENT_HZ" -ge 165 ]; then
    TARGET_FPS=165
    ANIM_FACTOR=0.35
elif [ "$CURRENT_HZ" -ge 120 ]; then
    TARGET_FPS=144
    ANIM_FACTOR=0.40
else
    TARGET_FPS=120 # Virtual 120 for 60Hz monitors
    ANIM_FACTOR=0.45
fi

echo "[2/4] Applying Adaptive Display Config (${TARGET_FPS} FPS)..."
kwriteconfig6 --file kwinrc --group "Compositing" --key "MaxFPS" $TARGET_FPS
kwriteconfig6 --file kwinrc --group "Compositing" --key "RefreshRate" $TARGET_FPS
kwriteconfig6 --group "KWin" --key "AnimationDurationFactor" $ANIM_FACTOR

echo "[3/4] Thermal Control Policy (Laptop/Tablet Optimized)..."
# Balance CPU to prevent heat spikes
sudo cat <<EOF > /usr/local/bin/hok-mode
#!/bin/bash
# High-Efficiency Gaming Mode
echo "schedutil" | sudo tee /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu*/cpufreq/scaling_governor
# Limit GPU power draw to prevent overheating
echo "auto" | sudo tee /sys/class/drm/card0/device/power_dpm_force_performance_level
notify-send "HoKOS" "OPTIMIZED FOR ${CURRENT_HZ}Hz | MODE: COOL & SMOOTH" -i hok_logo
EOF
sudo chmod +x /usr/local/bin/hok-mode

echo "[4/4] Branding & SFX..."
sudo cp ./assets/branding_logo.svg /usr/share/plasma/look-and-feel/aero/contents/images/start.svg
# Map Apple macOS Tahoe Sounds on startup and Microsoft Windows XP Sounds off
echo "aplay /usr/share/sounds/mac_bong.wav &" >> ~/.config/autostart-scripts/boot.sh

echo "HoKOS v1.4 INSTALLED SUCCESSFULLY."
